# ============================================================================================
# scratch/ -- the probes stay, what they produced does not
# ============================================================================================
#
# `scratch/` is 3.5 GB across ~1,270 files and it holds three different things. Only one of them is
# code, and the rules below are written so that the split is by KIND rather than by a list of paths
# somebody has to remember to extend:
#
#   1. ~1,200 .py probe scripts. THESE ARE THE REPRODUCTION PATH, not leftovers. 217 distinct scratch
#      paths are cited by name from docs/, examples/paper/ and stable_envs/ source comments ("measured
#      by scratch/census/bbox_probe.py"), and `tests/unit/test_repo_contracts.py` re-extracts every one
#      of those citations and fails if it stops resolving or if a rule here starts ignoring it.
#      No EXTENSION rule below matches a .py, a .sh, a .sbatch or a .md, so a probe cannot be caught by
#      one; the two directory rules (3 and the named vendored trees in 4) can, and each was checked
#      against the tree before it was written. The test is what keeps that true.
#
#   2. What the probes PRODUCED -- 1,565 PNGs, 328 .npy, SLURM stdout, HTML frame dumps. Bulk and
#      regenerable: the script that wrote each one sits beside it. This is the evidence behind the
#      numbers and it belongs on disk, not in the history. A push to this repo has already failed on
#      1.7 GB of shards, and the standing rule is that the repo is code only.
#
#   3. Vendored upstream source that a probe had to build against -- `scratch/cule/` alone is 1,497
#      .hpp/.cu/.cpp files and 76 MB of somebody else's project.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED, and why: .json under a probe directory. They are the measured
# numbers themselves rather than a rendering of them, they total ~1.3 MB, and one of them
# (`scratch/census/union.json`, the 196-env census) is cited from README.md, docs/index.md,
# docs/benchmarks.md and examples/paper/main.tex. Output JSON that IS bulk lives under an `out/` or
# `results/` directory and is covered by the directory rules below.

# --- 1. rendered evidence and measurement arrays --------------------------------------------------
# Every one of these is written by a probe and re-written by re-running it. Images and video are the
# bulk (1,565 PNGs); the arrays are reference frames and qpos banks; the .html files are frame dumps
# (`scratch/altrender/frames.html` alone is 0.9 MB of base64).
scratch/**/*.png
scratch/**/*.jpg
scratch/**/*.jpeg
scratch/**/*.webp
scratch/**/*.gif
scratch/**/*.mp4
scratch/**/*.pdf
scratch/**/*.html
scratch/**/*.npy
scratch/**/*.npz
scratch/**/*.pt
scratch/**/*.pth
scratch/**/*.ckpt
scratch/**/*.safetensors
scratch/**/*.parquet
scratch/**/*.arrow
scratch/**/*.lance/
scratch/**/*.mjb

# --- 2. run logs ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLURM stdout is named `<job>.<id>.out` here. `*.log` is already ignored globally, further up.
scratch/**/*.out
scratch/**/*.err
scratch/**/logs/
scratch/**/nohup.out

# --- 3. probe output directories ------------------------------------------------------------------
# By convention a probe writes under `out/` or `results/` beside itself. Checked: no .py lives under
# either in this tree, so these cannot swallow a cited probe. `scratch/robocasa/out/corpus/` (3 GB of
# expanded MJCFs, qpos banks and union models, rebuilt by `scratch/robocasa/dump_corpus.py` in ~15 min
# on a GPU node) and `scratch/ogbench/out/` are the two big ones; both are cited from docs as the
# place the raw numbers live, and test_repo_contracts.py records them as regenerable rather than
# letting the citation quietly rot.
scratch/*/out/
scratch/*/outputs/
scratch/*/results/

# --- 4. vendored upstream source ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not ours and not written here. The extension rules are the general case -- nothing in this
# repository authors C or C++, verified over every tracked file -- so the next vendored tree is
# excluded the day it lands instead of after it is pushed. The named directories stay because they
# also carry Python, assets and build systems that the extensions do not reach: 32 MB of
# `openai/procgen` C++ and assets that `scratch/procgen/probe13_recon.py`'s header explains how to
# re-fetch in one curl, the two CuLE forks and a CUDA-10-era Thrust tree the replay measurement had to
# build against, and the pixelbrax / kage-bench checkouts.
scratch/**/*.cu
scratch/**/*.cuh
scratch/**/*.cpp
# ...except this one. RAYCAST-3's micro-benchmark kernel is a hand-written SOURCE, not build output:
# examples/results/step6/raycast3d/findings.md cites it, and the whole go/no-go it reports is whether
# that transcription is bit-identical to cast_nearest_torch -- which a reviewer can only judge by
# reading it. The blanket rule above is for compiled artifacts.
!scratch/step6/raycast3d/cast_kernel.cpp
scratch/**/*.cc
scratch/**/*.hpp
scratch/**/*.h
scratch/**/*.inl
# Vendored MESH assets, which are the same thing in a different file format. 56 files and 66 MB of
# MuJoCo Menagerie UR5e arm and Robotiq gripper geometry under `scratch/backend3d/scenes/` (and a
# second copy of all of it under `scenes/flat/`), pulled in so the four hand-written .xml scenes
# beside them have something to load. The scenes are ours and are cited; the meshes are upstream's.
scratch/**/*.obj
scratch/**/*.stl
scratch/**/*.dae
scratch/**/*.mtl
scratch/**/*.ply
scratch/**/*.msh
scratch/**/*.skn
scratch/procgen/_src/
scratch/cule/cule_mehrdad/
scratch/cule/cule_chengscott/
scratch/cule/thrust_1_9_10/
scratch/cule/cudahome/
scratch/gpunative/pixelbrax/
scratch/gpunative/kage-bench/
scratch/cule/get-pip.py

# --- 5. probe scenes that ARE inputs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The four backend3d scenes are cited by docs/research/backend3d.md and are hand-written MJCF, not
# output; rule 1 does not touch .xml, and this says so out loud so nobody adds an .xml rule later.
!scratch/backend3d/scenes/*.xml

# ============================================================================================
# examples/ -- build artefacts
# ============================================================================================
# `examples/paper/` is a LaTeX project whose source (main.tex, tables/*.tex, the .sty files it
# vendors) is tracked and whose build output is not. `examples/results/*.json` are the measured tables
# themselves -- small, cited by examples/paper/make_tables.py and by tests/unit/test_benchmarks.py --
# and stay. `examples/lewm_pusht/logs/` is covered by that directory's own .gitignore.
examples/paper/main.pdf
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.bbl
*.blg
